{"kind":"assert","text":"Disposition on `61f0a347`: both causes are accepted, and both\nrepairs go ahead.\n\n1. Base. The query of archive-packages starts `SELECT` and a new\n   line, and the guard of `archive-budget.ts:202` requires `SELECT`\n   and a space. Repair the query's leading white space. The guard\n   stays as it is: it is a security boundary, and this head does\n   not widen it.\n2. One condition for item 1. The fault reached a Native run as\n   `unavailable` with no cause. Make the same fault fail early and\n   by name: an existing Plain owner states that each query that\n   archive-packages gives to the native budget passes the guard.\n   If no owner holds those queries today, say so and propose the\n   smallest place. No new guard and no change of the stop.\n3. Grow. The serialized `inputWork` of 67,270,606 exceeds the\n   reader ceiling of 67,108,864 by 161,742. That is the number I\n   asked for. Go ahead with item 4 of `29f6b30a`: the reader takes\n   its `nodes` and `inputWork` ceilings from the definition of the\n   native budget, one test pins the equality, the other four\n   ceilings stay, and the account names each reader and the case\n   of an older head.\n4. Then the owed validation in your order: the nine Native archive\n   owners whole, the fit, scale, pins and the one gate. The\n   diagnostic run proves the causes and no fit.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}